    "t_cal": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "x": 0,
      "y": 8060,
      "maxW": 4240,
      "text": "Proposed (§25): a calendar that scrolls"
    },
    "n_cal": {
      "x": -560,
      "y": 8360,
      "w": 480,
      "size": 24,
      "text": "One column of weeks that scrolls up and down, months running into each other. Six weeks in view; it opens on the selected date's month, as the paged grid did, and keeps going either way. Snaps to a week when it comes to rest.\n\nThe prototype (left) has the strip's Calendar and Scroll switches; the prototype at the top still opens the paged grid, as built.\n\nTry: scroll with the trackpad; ↑↓←→; Page Up and Page Down; type “mar 3”; scroll far and press Today."
    }
